      "timestamp": "2026-08-30T22:31:37.471175+00:00",
      "type": "understanding",
      "summary": "Agent explained goal and mechanics.",
      "understanding": {
        "goal_understanding": "Navigate the grid to complete each level by activating and then stepping onto every goal cell. A goal cell can only be completed when the carried piece exactly matches that goal\u2019s required shape, color, and rotation at the same time; once all goals in the level are completed, you advance, and finishing all levels wins the game.",
        "mechanics_understanding": "Each turn you choose a movement action (MOVE_NORTH/SOUTH/EAST/WEST). Moving normally costs stamina; if stamina reaches zero you lose a life, and losing all lives ends the game. The grid contains walls that can block movement. Stepping on modifier tiles changes the carried piece: shape modifiers cycle the piece\u2019s shape, color modifiers cycle its color, and rotation modifiers rotate it 90\u00b0 clockwise. When your piece matches a goal\u2019s requirements, that goal becomes activated, and you must then move onto the goal cell to complete it."
      }
